(LST2-21 — list elements are reached by `element N of <list>` and are
 1-indexed: element 1 is the first item. The manual's own "List Element
 Access" block, verbatim.
 Also covers: LST2-22 (a literal index), LST2-23 (`'s first`/`'s last` in
 Print position agree with element 1 and element N), LST2-24 (a variable
 index works and reads the same slot a literal would).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST2-21.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   10
   20
   10
   30
   20
)
a list called nums is [10, 20, 30].

Print element 1 of nums.
Print element 2 of nums.
Print nums's first.
Print nums's last.

(Using variable index)
a number called i is 2.
Print element i of nums.
